the first person to go on trial on  charges from the assault on the capitol  has been convicted on all counts it was  a pivotal victory for the justice  department because it could create a  blueprint for trying hundreds of cases  like it scott mcfarland has reaction to  the verdict in the trial where  prosecutors had almost all of the  evidence on their side  it took the jury less than four hours to  convict guy refered to texas on five  counts including carrying a gun to the  capitol grounds obstruction of congress  and interfering with police he now  potentially faces up to 60 years in  prison  for days prosecutors showed jurors a  series of videos and photos of revit at  the front of the mob on january 6 2021  though he never made it inside the  capitol  his own son testified against refit  saying he was so frightened by his  father's anti-government rhetoric that  he tipped off the fbi and he pointed to  messages in which refit bragged after  the riot i felt so  patriotic and felt like such an american  girl we did  refit didn't testify and his lawyers  didn't present any witnesses one juror  spoke with us after the verdict asking  we not reveal her identity did that  matter to you at all that this man  didn't take the stand and didn't present  a defense  it did it did  the one time that we saw any emotion out  of him was when his son took the stand  so yeah it did it mattered a lot  prosecutors didn't just win this case  they potentially won new leverage over  those still awaiting trial  there will be many defendants who've  seen this verdict  saw how it was returned quickly  unanimously the strength of the  government's case and they're going to  seek a plea deal and they're going to  seek cooperation as part of that after  the verdict refit's wife told me she  hopes other defendants are not scared  into taking pleas  the reason that we have all guilty  verdicts is they are making a point out  of guy  there's also a new high profile january  6 defendant proud boys leader enrique  tario was arrested on tuesday and  appeared in a miami court charged with  conspiracy he didn't take part in the  riot but prosecutors say he helped plan  and direct the mob  tario's attorney tells me they have no  comment but are back in court friday as  for guy refit his wife says they plan to  appeal this verdict but sentencing in  the meantime is set for june 8.  nate  scott thank you
 

